# Cloudflare Pages redirects
#
# Defensive: Cloudflare Pages can fall back to serving the homepage
# HTML for any path that doesn't match a static file (SPA-style
# catch-all). This is documented behavior and shows up on
# myhotradar.com: a request to /radar/latest.json returns the
# homepage with Content-Type text/html when the file is not yet
# deployed.
#
# To guarantee the JSON artifact is served with its real Content-Type
# (application/json), we add explicit self-redirect rules for the
# known public asset paths. These rules are no-ops when the file
# exists (the static asset serves directly), but they force the
# catch-all to step aside if the path would otherwise rewrite.
#
# See the static-site-mvp skill: Cloudflare Pages doesn't 404
# missing paths — it falls back to index.html with text/html.
#
# Format reference:
#   https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/

# Radar Feed JSON artifact (Phase 2 B3B-1)
/radar/latest.json   /radar/latest.json   200
